<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gipuzkoa</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Guipúzcoa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gipuzkoa is the smallest province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and one of the three provinces of the Basque Country, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-biscay">Bay of Biscay</a> along the French border, with its capital at San Sebastián. Long part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Kingdom of Navarre</a>'s sphere, it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> in 1200 while keeping its own charters (fueros). It became a centre of shipbuilding, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-technology">ironworking</a> and later industry, and Basque is widely spoken there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gipuzkoa.jpg" alt="Gipuzkoa" width="320" height="275" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gipuzkoa_in_Spain_(plus_Canarias).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
